 "description": "NON-RIGID DEFORMATION INVARIANCE (FRONTIER rung T4): recognition under SMOOTH non-rigid deformation, BOUNDED by the identity-preservation bound so that a small smooth warp (handwriting -- a letter written differently is the SAME letter) is recognized while a deformation large enough to CHANGE identity (a strong shear, MEASURED identity-changing in VISION_SIMILARITY_RESULTS) is REFUSED. Two rules df_recognize / df_refuse over the held SmoothDeformComponents Term, gated on the NEW flag agent.deform (OFF by default -> committed bench byte-identical). NO new Rust. See VISION_DEFORMATION_RESULTS.md for the measured outcome, including which clauses of the bound are load-bearing and which are inert (sec 13.2).",
 "microtheory": "vision",
 "nodes": [],
 "edges": [],
