  {
   "name": "df_recognize",
   "comment": "NON-RIGID DEFORMATION, recognize branch (flag deform==1). codebook-proposes / deformation-verdict-decides, BOUNDED: the ShapeSignature codebook proposes the identity set; the held SmoothDeformComponents Term (deform_metric.rs:255) fits SmoothDeformDist's OWN free-form-deformation field between each candidate's dense point set and the observation and DECOMPOSES it into an affine part (rotation/shear/log_scale) plus the NON-AFFINE 'bending' residual. covered_by = Argmin over candidates of DictGet(...,'total') -- 'total' is the Term's own fused verdict, byte-identical to SmoothDeformDist. Recognized iff the winner satisfies THE IDENTITY-PRESERVATION BOUND, whose three clauses are ALL generated by ONE falls-out quantity (VISION_PROTOCOL sec 13): eps = (sqrt(2)/2)/R, the integer-lattice HALF-DIAGONAL expressed in unit-RMS-normalized units, R the codebook's own mean RMS radius -- the identical constant continuous pose used, for the identical reason (a quantized observation certifies a point's position only to the lattice half-diagonal). total <= eps (linear in displacement); Abs(shear) <= eps (INHERITED from VISION_SIMILARITY_RESULTS: identity-preserving <=> M.Mt = lambda I <=> shear 0, identifiable only to observational resolution -- the shears are MEASURED identity-changing); bending <= eps^2 (a mean SQUARED displacement, so the floor squared). eps is graph data on the agent (df_eps), written by the adapter from the held codebook's own geometry exactly as continuous pose wrote cp_angles -- measured, never fitted. Fires only on status=='df_decoded', so with the flag absent NEITHER df rule fires and the sd loop is byte-identical (sec 9). NO new Rust: SmoothDeformComponents/DictGet/Argmin/Abs/Lte/Times/Attr/NodesOfType all pre-exist (VISION_DEFORMATION_PREREG sec 1).",
